{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/444657-a-question-about-legion-and-guild-allegiance","id":444657,"title":"A question about Legion and Guild allegiance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-16T12:12:42-07:00","id":444657,"title":"A question about Legion and Guild allegiance","content":"Dear forumites and fellow lovers of Wraith!<br /> <br /> I finally, after about a decade of longing and trying and failed attempts, got to play Wraith, albeit in the ST seat.<br /> <br /> I have a few questions about the day-to-day society of Wraith. Lets assume all of this is pre Ends Of Empire (or in the new continuity)<br /> <br /> How does Legion and Guild allegiance actually work? I understand that the Beggar Lord does get some &quot;leftover&quot; souls, or some that cant be decided upon by the other Deathlords. But how do deathmarks figure into this, then? Are deathmarks more like suggestions than laws/rules? Similarly, I remember a couple of story pages from Wraith:TGW about how the dead from the Spanish Flu would now go and fatten the numbers of the Loyalist Legions. But why wait? Maelstrom notwithstanding, why not just reap all freshly crossed souls if you control a Necropolis and its an all out war? Even the Book of Legions has a prefab Silent Legion character who has specifically not dies by suicide. I currently treat the Legions more as suggestions and groups held together by interests than by death type, as that fits better with my &quot;well, now you are dead, what do you do?&quot; story/frame.<br /> <br /> Similarly, what about Guilds? I get that they are guilds in the medieval sense, a group and organisation centred around the usage of a specific Arcanos. But can you be a member of several Guilds? Are Guilds more like occupational schools and unions, or are do they claim membership of all the practitioners of their respective Arcanos? One of my players has dots in all three &quot;entertainment&quot; Arcanoi (Keening, Moliate, Phantasm). What Guild would she canonically belong to? I run them as universities and opt-in unions, but I'd like to know the canon version.<br /> <br /> Also, how do Necropoli look in the &quot;canon&quot;? Are they reflective of the current era of the city, or are they the sum of all destroyed, decayed, abandoned, demolished buildings with enough attachment to cross over? Is it in canon to introduce the multidmensional and fluid (of sorts) nature of Stygia, the city, into Shadowlands Necropoli? That is more or less what I'm doing currently, with Detroit being made up of all those abandoned and destroyed hotels and office buildings and the occasional industrial park turned renegade stomping ground and/or foundry.<br /> <br /> Best Wishes<br /> <br /> Herbert West<br /> The Reanimator","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T07:37:07-07:00","id":445809,"title":"","content":"Hey Herbert,<br /> <br /> Welcome to the fracas! Nice to see I'm not the newest forumite now.<br /> <br /> Well, in theory, the legions can contest/fight over wraiths (and they often do). Usually a necropolis has representatives from multiple legions, so they'll all be out looking for bodies. But I'd imagine certain legions will be more likely to hang around certain locations than others (cancer wards, warzones, suicide hotspots). They might also use Arcanoi (I'm thinking Fatalism here) to see how certain individuals might die, and then follow them around for a while. Many reapers will be freelance too, and turn the wraiths they find into the relevant legion (based on their deathmarks) for a nice reward. In theory, though, any legion could reap a wraith and claim them as their own--but will the wraith play ball? And will the other legions notice and kick up a fuss?<br /> <br /> Guilds are more like secret societies, or criminal organisations like the Triads or the Mafia. They're underground and they have inititation rites, etc. It's not easy to join one, and they only want the 'right' people on their side. They try to control the best arts for themselves, although there are lots of people practising Arcanoi throughout Stygia (but they'll probably only know the lower level, most common arts). That means a wraith is unlikely to be a member of more than one Guild, as any such wraith would probably be a double-agent or an exposure risk. Guilds wouldn't want their secrets getting out, after all. In such instances, a wraith would choose their 'official' Guild membership (if they have one at all), but it might draw suspicion if they're equally good in all Arcanoi at high levels ('Who taught you that?' 'Why are you distracting yourself with learning that Arcanos when you could be focusing on this one?' Etc.).<br /> <br /> Necropoli are a combination of both the 'current era of the city' and 'the sum of all destroyed, decayed, abandoned, demolished buildings with enough attachment to cross over'. Think of it this way: the foundations resemble the city as it currently is, and are slightly hazy/'unreal' to wraiths because these parts of the city are just intrusions into the Shadowlands from across the Shroud; then the bits on top are the more solid, 'real' (to a wraith) elements composed of relics and artifacts. These latter parts are all the things that have crossed over or are made of souls. A wraith can walk through the 'unreal' bits (at the cost of one corpus), but the wraithly bits (those bits that lie firmly on the dead side of the Shroud) are solid to them. So yes, your approach sounds right, I'm trying to say :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:09:17-07:00","id":446737,"title":"","content":"Those &quot;hazy parts&quot;? They're the ones that will get you. 1 Corpus every time you walk through a Skinlands wall. <br /> <br /> Of course, you can't just walk one through the walls of all the Relic buildings that have &quot;crossed over&quot;, so there's that at least. <br /> <br /> So... Skinlands buildings = tough jello, Shadowland buildings = rocks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}